Qt Network security fixes for the exact Linux Qt 6.10.2 ABI.

Upstream Qt advisories and patches:
https://www.qt.io/blog/security-advisory-cve-2026-105946
https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.11/CVE-2026-105946-qtbase-6.11-0001.diff
https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.11/CVE-2026-105946-qtbase-6.11-0002.diff
https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.11/CVE-2026-105946-qtbase-6.11-0003.diff
https://www.qt.io/blog/security-advisory-cve-2026-95620
https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.11/CVE-2026-95620-qtbase-6.11.diff
https://www.qt.io/blog/security-advisory-cve-2026-96432
https://download.qt.io/official_releases/qt/6.11/CVE-2026-96432-qtbase-6.11.diff

The NTLM production hunks apply unchanged. HTTP/2 hunks retain the 6.10.2
string literals. No public API or class layout changes. Upstream tests are
not copied into the dependency build, which has tests disabled.

